---
import Section from './Section.astro';
import TermPanel from './system/TermPanel.astro';
import CheckRow from './system/CheckRow.astro';
import VerdictBadge from './system/VerdictBadge.astro';
// Move 4. The product, condensed. The full walkthrough lives in the methodology;
// this is the homepage version. Four checks, the sealed container, three
// verdicts, and the line that makes the verdict worth anything.
const checks = [
  { n: '01', name: 'Closed', body: 'Re-scan after the patch. Is the reported finding actually gone, or did it move?' },
  { n: '02', name: 'Hole shut', body: 'Fire attacks the fixer never saw. One that still lands is a failure.' },
  { n: '03', name: 'Behaviour held', body: 'Every ordinary input still works, matched against a known-correct reference. A legitimate value the fix now rejects is a failure.' },
  { n: '04', name: 'Provenance clean', body: 'No suppression, no new finding, no alert closed while attacks still land.' },
];
---

<Section id="checks" tint>
  <h2 class="h2 reveal">Four checks, in a sealed container.</h2>

  <p class="reveal body mt-8" style="--reveal-delay:60ms">
    The patch is applied to a clean checkout and scored with no network egress, torn down
    between patches. Three of the checks are the ordinary questions any careful team asks. The
    two that catch real failures run inputs the fixer never saw: attacks the hole must still
    block, and legitimate values it must still accept.
  </p>

  <div class="reveal mt-10" style="--reveal-delay:60ms">
    <TermPanel path="assay · the four checks">
      {checks.map((ch) => <CheckRow id={ch.n} name={ch.name} desc={ch.body} state="pending" status="" />)}
    </TermPanel>
  </div>

  <p class="reveal mt-8 note" style="--reveal-delay:120ms;max-width:62ch">
    If you let a student write their own exam, they will pass it. You test them on
    questions they have not seen.
  </p>

  <div class="reveal mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-8 gap-y-8 lg:grid-cols-2" style="--reveal-delay:60ms">
    <div>
      <p class="hd mb-4">Three verdicts</p>
      <p class="body">
        <VerdictBadge label="VERIFIED" tone="pass" />,{' '}
        <VerdictBadge label="NOT VERIFIED" tone="fail" />, and{' '}
        <VerdictBadge label="INSUFFICIENT EVIDENCE" tone="neutral" />. The third is a
        first-class verdict, reported rather than dropped. A result we cannot stand behind is
        worth more than one we invent, and that is the point.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="border-t border-line pt-8 lg:border-l lg:border-t-0 lg:pl-8 lg:pt-0">
      <p class="hd mb-4">Why the verdict is worth anything</p>
      <p class="body">
        We do not write fixes. The thing being checked and the thing doing the checking are
        never the same party. Independence is the whole product.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="disc reveal mt-12 border-t border-line pt-6" style="--reveal-delay:60ms">
    Works with any scanner and any fixer. SARIF in, verdict out.
  </p>
</Section>
